Performance tests (test/performance)
====================================

Status on 2026-11-13, checked with gfortran, CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Fast and
OpenBLAS, single-threaded, for both master (2ce4fd2a9) and the sguga_III
branch (production code path, MOLCAS_CI_VERIFY unset). Tests checked:
900-906, 913, 915, 916, 918. Not run: 907, 908, 909-912, 914, 917.

Known problems, identical on master and sguga_III (so not caused by the
branch). TO BE HANDLED IN THE FUTURE:

* 902  FAILS: E_CASPT2 = -909.4082221283, checkfile -909.4081192475,
       error 1.0e-4 with tolerance 1.0e-8. E_SCF and E_RASSCF agree. The
       CASPT2 reference value (or the test setup) needs to be checked and
       the checkfile updated if the new value is confirmed.

* 918  passes, but takes about 16-17 minutes instead of the "about 2 min 15 sec"
       stated in the input; nearly all of it is ALASKA (11-13 minutes). This
       is not a regression: at the commit that added the test (d3f477a99,
       2026-07-01) it takes 940 s with the same build settings (seward 142 s,
       rasscf 37 s, caspt2 64 s, mclr 7 s, alaska 680 s). The estimate in the
       input header was wrong from the start; it now says about 16 min.
       (If a short test was the intention, the test should be made cheaper.)

* The "Runtime:" estimates in the input headers are outdated: on current
  hardware most tests take a fraction of the stated time (e.g. 900 takes
  about 27 s instead of about 3 min).

Timing comparison master vs sguga_III, one test at a time on an idle
machine (wall time in seconds, two runs each):

  test   master       sguga_III
  900    27.4  27.6   27.2  27.0
  901    12.3  12.4   12.4  12.5
  903     8.3   8.3    8.3   8.3
  904     9.6   9.6    9.6   9.6
  905    25.5  25.6   25.3  25.2
  906     9.4   9.5    9.4   9.4
  915    13.1  13.1   13.0  13.1

i.e. no difference beyond about 1%. (Before the fix in SG_Init, which now
leaves the determinant reordering SDREO to be built on first use,
sguga_III took 16.2 s for 904, a CAS(12,12), against 9.7 s on master.)
